{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"90680527-362a-4296-aa12-b8ea89bb9ebc","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root‑The root‑cause analysis and the applied fixes are documented in **[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/90680527-362aa-4296-aa12-b8ea89bb9ebc/ANSWER.md)**.\n\nKey points applied:\n\n* Replaced the illegal `status=$?` assignment with a safe `rc=$?`.\n* Added the missing `USER` environment variable to the launchd plist.\n* Piped the multi‑line prompt to Claude via stdin (`print … | claude -p - …`) to avoid prompt‑parsing failures.\n* Updated the script accordingly (see the edited `bin/nightly-review.zsh`).  \n\nThese changes resolve the silent launchd job, eliminate the “read‑only variable: status” errors, and allow Claude to run correctly under launchd, restoring both success and failure notifications.\n","duration_seconds":125.030949,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":33291,"output_tokens":11486,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":477760,"total_tokens":44777}}}
